WEBVTT

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:12.620
Walking in the woods one day Chris and Martin saw something strange

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.160
A little leaping lemur who liked to bounce and play

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.220
They followed their new bouncing friend Not knowing where this adventure would end

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.770
The animals were headed just around the bend

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.620
I don't know

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.740
How do we get there?

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:29.540
Come on, let's go

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.260
And use a boost to see

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:19.950
We've been Creature Adventuring in a Batcave.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.640
Boy, do we smell like bat guano.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.810
Bat guano is bat poop.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.970
And bat guano smells big time.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:29.650
Hey, let's call Zabu.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:42.250
Hey, Zabu, you must have smelled this all the way in the forest.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.270
You know Zabu, no chat until after he's had a snack.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.620
What do you think's in the snack machine?

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:59.980
Oh, and there you go.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.860
We all love bananas.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.420
Okay, one more little piece.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:05.930
There you go.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:19.020
I love bananas.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:23.380
Smell.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:25.320
Smell.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:25.800
Different.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.000
Well, not the same.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.070
Not like Chris.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:28.990
Not like Martin.

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:29.850
That's because...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.860
We have the smell of guano on us.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.140
Guano? Guano?

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.190
What's guano?

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:35.880
Poop.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:36.540
Poop.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.320
Not all creatures like the smell of bat poop,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.700
but most creatures are really curious about how other creatures smell.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.700
I saw a creature in the forest.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.960
Smell, smell, sniff, sniff.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.170
That's what he did.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:51.650
Who could it be?

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.960
Be this animal who I didn't see.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.900
Can you help me guess this news?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.300
One big body?

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.280
What a nose!

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.840
This is nose to eat with!

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:36.020
This animal who I see, can you help me guess this?

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:40.400
Miz, a big, long-nosed creature.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:41.800
Do you know who he is?

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.160
Long, snaky nose.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:47.480
Big, floppy ears.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:48.740
Big, round feet.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:49.740
Tiny eyes.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:51.140
Really, really heavy.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:51.960
Little tail.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.230
It's a baby elephant.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.580
Honka Zika, mystery animal's here.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:58.640
Wow.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:03:59.260
Hey.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:00.560
How you doing?

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.200
A baby effluent?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:04.640
Elephant, Zob.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:06.910
Elephant.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:08.010
Elephant.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:09.710
Hey, elephant.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.470
I think he's interested in our guano smell.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:17.470
Maybe he followed our smell all the way to Animal Junction.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.600
Wow, look at these feet.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:21.210
See, these are the toes.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:26.010
One, two, three, four, and five.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.960
These are the toenails.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:35.080
The bottom of an elephant's foot is like one big, soft pad.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.330
This helps an elephant walk really quietly,

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:40.650
even though he's so big.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:50.170
Unch, Zika, your hair is hard.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:55.180
Yeah, the hair that covers an elephant's body

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:59.220
is hard and bristly, like a toothbrush.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.760
But this toothbrush is more his size.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.440
Let's give him a good back scratch.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.340
Yes, that is good, yeah.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:14.520
Oh, I'm going to scratch right behind his ears.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.520
Hey, Chris, try that on me.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:17.760
Sure, Zob.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.120
Oh, that feels good.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:22.420
Oh, lower down my back.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:23.000
OK.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.380
Oh, oh, oh.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:25.340
How's that, Zob?

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:25.820
Oh, yeah.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.060
Harder, harder, harder, harder.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.120
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:29.890
You OK?

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:42.160
I can't cover that much elephant with this little toothbrush, so I have to do the detail

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:42.520
work.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.140
How does that feel?

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:45.610
Why?

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:47.540
Hard with a small toothbrush.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.450
Hey, look at the elephant's tail.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.780
It's kind of like a toothbrush too.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.360
See those bristles?

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.740
It's a scratchin'.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.550
There's a lot of elephant to cover.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.060
And he loves being scratched with a toothbrush.

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:05.720
Hey, can I call you Toothbrush?

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.400
Toothbrush, that's a great name, Zob.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:11.200
A good toothbrush scratch for Toothbrush.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.420
Yup, and we scratched him from top to bottom.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:18.860
An elephant has one of the most incredible noses.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:21.010
It's called a trunk.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:22.480
Trunk?

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:23.680
Trunk.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.880
His trunk is longer than my whole body.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.920
And Toothbrush can do incredible things.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.240
with this nose.

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:33.550
Can he blow a goopleberry off his nose?

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.210
What are you doing?

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.360
Hey, you smell in my shoes.

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:42.900
An elephant uses his nose to help him talk.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:51.780
To make all kinds of sounds.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:54.100
When they're excited or surprised, they trumpet.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.000
Well, he can tickle with his nose, too.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.260
That's right, Tom.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.600
An elephant uses his nose to explore.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.800
Hey, what's he doing with harmonica?

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.780
Brush, you're playing the harmonica.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:26.080
Harmonica.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:29.040
An elephant's nose is always up to something.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:29.860
What a nose.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.160
The elephant can grab on to things with his trunk.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.740
Just call me trunk fingers.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:43.360
I wish my nose could grab on to things and reach out.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.480
It's like having an arm and a hand on your face.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:48.820
What a nose.

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:58.190
The way he uses his nose as a straw.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.980
He sucks water up.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.560
into his nose, and then blows it out into his mouth.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.440
That's the way an elephant drinks, with his nose.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:09.690
Creature who drinks with his nose?

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:11.400
I can't believe my mind.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:23.040
Oh, another amazing thing an elephant can do with his nose,

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:24.600
use it as a hose.

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:26.260
Toothbrush gave you a shower.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:26.980
Yeah.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:29.960
Elephant spray the .

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.160
and each other to keep cool.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.800
Nothing feels better than a cool shower

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.740
on a hot African afternoon.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:43.940
Have a look at this.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:44.560
Whoa!

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:45.520
Wow!

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:50.810
You're supposed to kick it.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:53.110
He's trying to eat the soccer ball.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.600
Can't believe my mind.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:57.540
Kick that ball!

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:58.980
Let's play.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.440
Hey, he's really good at this.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:04.920
Coming at ya!

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:05.590
Yeah!

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:10.910
I wonder who taught him to play soccer.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:16.550
Nice kick, Toothbrush!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:22.710
Thanks, Toothbrush!

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:27.320
Oh, that reminds me of something that happened in Zabu Land.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.490
I was leaping along.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.710
Leap, leap, leap, when all of a sudden, I heard a sniffling sound.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:39.930
I took one big leap and landed next to Narchie, who was standing next to Goobel and crying.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:43.410
What's the matter, Narchie? Why are you crying?

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:49.830
We're trying to play catch with the Goobelberry, but I can't throw, because my arms are too stubby.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:57.240
Well, I said we could play another game, Marta. He wants to play catch.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.300
I've got an idea, Narchie. Don't use your arms to throw.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.500
Use your nose and blow.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:07.140
Oh, good idea.

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.120
Good idea, huh? I'm ready.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.340
Hey, here we go.

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:14.260
And I'm the lemur in the middle.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:20.020
It worked. I can play.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.260
Let's do it again.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:22.820
Yeah, yeah, go ahead.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:26.180
So we played Gooboo Berry Catch all day.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:27.980
And I was the lemur in the middle.

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:33.460
Yeah, but here, catch!

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:34.310
The end.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.340
Chris, Martin, toothbrush is hungry.

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:41.320
You want to eat those?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.380
We have a lot better stuff.

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:44.800
Come over here to the food machine.

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:46.370
All right, so what do you want?

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:48.390
Okay, you know, you don't want that.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:49.250
That's for a coati.

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:51.090
This is for a porcupine.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.870
Let's see here.

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:55.290
How about, I know we have stuff for elephants.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:57.110
Can you back up a little bit?

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:59.010
Hey, right over here, elephant stuff.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:10:59.890
See that?

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.100
There we go. Push it together.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:06.500
Uh-oh.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:09.120
Uh-oh, Chris, it's on the fritz again.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:09.740
Uh-oh.

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:10.680
Not again.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:11.940
I'll get the tools.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:14.320
Yeah, we'll fix it up to feed an elephant.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:15.280
Hold it, Martin.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:16.780
Look at that.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.280
Toothbrush has an idea.

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:22.200
Your nose.

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:23.420
Good idea, toothbrush.

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:28.160
Whoa, look at that trunk go.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.090
Well, I guess he fixed it himself.

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:36.690
That's an amazing thing about an elephant's nose.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:38.950
Hey, you know, this is too much work, though.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:40.730
We still got to fix this machine.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:41.030
Yeah.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.930
At this rate, he'll never fill his belly.

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:46.280
Man, toothbrush has a big belly.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.520
Because elephants need a lot of food.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:51.960
When an elephant's hungry and wants some leaves,

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:54.120
she might push down the whole tree.

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:58.480
Her nose goes into action.

00:11:58.890 --> 00:11:59.970
Picking in over three...

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.720
of food in one day.

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:06.210
Hang on there, toothbrush.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:09.810
Yeah, we just have to fix this thing up to feed an elephant.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.840
We're ready, let's give it a try.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:26.250
Now this is what an elephant needs, a lot of food.

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:29.880
It's as much as a dinosaur.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.040
Here you go.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:36.340
Marks that apple.

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:41.500
I'm already full, but he just keeps on eating.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.400
Let's watch this apple go from the elephant's trunk

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:46.520
into his mouth.

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:53.550
I love the sounds the elephant makes when he eats.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.400
You're the greatest toothbrush.

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:58.510
I'm feeling kind of elephant-ish.

00:12:58.970 --> 00:12:59.870
I'm feeling kind of a...

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:04.150
Feel different, not the same.

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:07.200
This kind of feeling I can't explain.

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:10.340
There's only one thing that I can do.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:12.490
I feel elephant-ish.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:14.890
How about you, elephant-ish?

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.020
Ella, Ella, elephant-ish.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:21.100
Elephant-ish.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:22.750
It tickles.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:26.150
I'm a long-nosed noser, nosing all around.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:43.560
Oh, Brushy's my elephant friend.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:44.620
Yeah, Zob.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.740
And elephants say hello to their friends with their trunks.

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:53.730
Ow.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:55.970
Toothbrush really likes Chris.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.790
Elephants are really social animals.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:13:59.970
That means they like...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:05.610
be together. They really don't like being on their own much. Elephants live together in groups,

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:11.970
and a group of elephants is called a herd. Where's his family? Hope he's not lost. He must have

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:17.120
wandered away from the herd when he followed his nose to Animal Junction. But the herd must be

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:29.960
close by, because everybody in the herd is after the baby elephants. Elephants are a lot longer

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:34.550
Like people, a young elephant stays with his mom

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:36.630
for a long, long time.

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:39.920
I think Toothbrush wants to go back to his herd soon.

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:42.220
What was that?

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:42.760
What?

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:43.350
Huh?

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:44.970
Money.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.040
Mungatzika.

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.460
Look at those wings.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:54.940
Woo.

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:57.000
Wow.

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:59.040
And look at that nose.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.880
A turkey vulture has the best sense of smell of any animal

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:04.660
in the world.

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:06.260
And look at this.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:08.440
You can see right through his nostril.

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:13.250
Hey, that message from Jackie must be around here somewhere.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:14.290
Here it is.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.990
All right, let's see what she's up to.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.320
From Jackie.

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:24.840
Why don't you guys come over and help me mow the lawn?

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:26.450
Kidding.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:29.880
It's me.

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:32.950
I can't cut the grass.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.460
There's lots of creatures that share in my backyard,

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:38.430
like the garter snake.

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:44.800
And sometimes if you share your yard,

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:46.360
you really have to share it.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:48.750
So I think I'll leave this part for my friends,

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.020
because I could always cut the grass later.

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:58.810
Snooter, I'd rather play with Snooter than mow the lawn anyway.

00:15:59.190 --> 00:15:59.790
Wouldn't you?

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:01.140
And you know what?

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:03.270
Dogs are great smellers.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:06.800
Great smellers?

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:08.910
Jackie just gave me a great idea.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.510
But there's no grass to cut, Martin.

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:11.570
Not that's up.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:14.490
I thought of a way that we could get toothbrush back

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:15.390
to the elephant herd.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:16.960
That's right.

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:18.940
All we have to do is call Myrtle.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:21.660
She's a bloodhound, and bloodhounds are one

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.080
of the best smellers around.

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:25.760
Yeah, and she can sniff her way all the way

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:26.780
to toothbrush's herd.

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:27.500
Great idea.

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:28.480
Let's call Myrtle.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:29.750
Let's do it.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:32.010
Myrtle!

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:33.080
